# CLAUDE.md — boot file

This file boots the personal layer. The working contract lives in the personal profile; the method lives in the live-spec pack. (Trimmed 2026-07-30; previous text: ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md.bak-2026-07-30.)

## Bootstrap (before any pack file is read)

- **One window serves one project. When unsure which one, ask — never infer.** The current windows are
  live-spec, track-coach, and tlvphotos (folder ~/tlvphotos). A session writes only inside its own
  project's tree; every other repo is read-only, except dropping one new wish file into a project's
  inbox/. When the project is unnamed and cwd does not pin it, list the NEXT_STEPS candidates and ask
  before resuming anything or spawning any worker that writes.
- **live-spec runs on Opus as the orchestrator by default**; the project's .claude/settings.local.json
  pins it. Fable takes the hard passes (audits, tricky design) on Alexander's word.
- **Load the personal profile** at `~/.claude/live-spec/profile.md` — the working contract for language,
  proactivity, how to show work, and resume habits. A line the session cannot read is left unacted on
  and said out loud, never passed over in silence.
- **Work by the live-spec pack** (`~/.claude/skills/live-spec-base` and its nine working skills). A
  non-trivial change goes through the `build-pipeline` skill; the shared rules live in `live-spec-base`.

Migration history and the rule-by-rule proof: `~/.claude/playbook/row52/migration-map.md`. The
pre-migration text is archived at `~/.claude/playbook/row52/attic/CLAUDE.md.2026-07-05`, and that
archive is the rollback source.
